//? Title: Hirschberg alignment: find a crossing, release the rows
//? Subtitle: Actual score profiles, tied optima and explicit score/output/history storage
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Align two entire byte strings while maximizing match, mismatch and linear gap
scores. A dense dynamic-programming table can recover an optimal path, but its
storage grows as the product of input lengths. Hirschberg recovers one optimum
by finding a crossing on a middle row and recursing on two subproblems. This
report follows actual split profiles, retains the original DNA-string example,
and distinguishes tied alignments from identical scores. The core now releases
parent rows before recursion, uses views instead of substring copies, and offers
shorter row orientation. Score arrays, recursive frames, output strings and
retained trace histories have separately stated costs.
)

\toc

> A tiny tie: AB versus BA

Use match 2, mismatch −1 and gap −2. Splitting AB after A gives three candidate
crossing columns in BA. Each has total score −2, so the preserved
first-maximizer rule selects j=0. The resulting alignment is AB− against −BA,
whereas dense Needleman–Wunsch can choose two mismatches, AB against BA, with
that same score. ASCII '-' in output means a gap; the mathematical minus glyph
in prose is only typography.

The table below comes from the producing forward/reverse sweeps. The concept
diagram plots the actual returned alignment as a grid path, with a chosen
crossing on the middle row. It does not reconstruct scores with a second
report-local DP implementation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hirschberg_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto t = dm::algorithms::hirschberg_trace("AB", "BA");
    const auto &r = t.splits.at(0);
    const auto nw = dm::algorithms::needleman_wunsch("AB", "BA");
    std::print("| candidate j | forward | reverse suffix | total | chosen |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "--- |\n");
    for (std::size_t j = 0; j < r.total.size(); ++j)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", j, r.forward[j],
                   r.reverse[j], r.total[j], j == r.b_mid);
    std::print("\nHirschberg score {}; rows `{}` / `{}`. Dense NW score {}; rows `{}` / `{}`. Selected " "crossing ({},{}).\n",
               t.run.alignment.score, t.run.alignment.a_aligned,
               t.run.alignment.b_aligned, nw.score, nw.a_aligned, nw.b_aligned,
               r.a_mid, r.b_mid);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d(180, 1000);
    dm::graphics::DiagramStroke grid;
    grid.color = {203, 213, 225};
    grid.width = 1;
    for (int i = 0; i <= 2; ++i) {
        d.path({{0, -double(i)}, {2, -double(i)}}, grid).path(
            {{double(i), 0}, {double(i), -2}}, grid);
        d.text({-.4, -double(i)}, std::format("i={}", i), 20).text(
            {double(i), .35}, std::format("j={}", i), 20);
    }
    auto middle = grid;
    middle.color = {220, 38, 38};
    middle.dashed = true;
    d.path({{-.1, -double(r.a_mid)}, {2.1, -double(r.a_mid)}}, middle);
    std::vector<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint> path{{0, 0}};
    std::size_t i = 0, j = 0;
    for (std::size_t k = 0; k < t.run.alignment.a_aligned.size(); ++k) {
        i += t.run.alignment.a_aligned[k] != '-';
        j += t.run.alignment.b_aligned[k] != '-';
        path.push_back({double(j), -double(i)});
    }
    dm::graphics::DiagramStroke chosen;
    chosen.color = {37, 99, 235};
    chosen.width = 3;
    chosen.arrow = true;
    d.path(path, chosen).ellipse({double(r.b_mid), -double(r.a_mid)}, .06, .06,
                                 {5, 150, 105}).text({1, 1.2},
                                                     "Actual path: all three split totals tie",
                                                     25).text(
        {1, -2.6},
        std::format("First maximum j={} → {} / {}", r.b_mid,
                    t.run.alignment.a_aligned, t.run.alignment.b_aligned), 22).save_svg("build/hirschberg_tiny.svg");
    if (r.b_mid != 0 || t.run.alignment.score != -2 || nw.score != -2)
        throw std::runtime_error("tiny ties");
}
```
