\caption(Peak score slots exclude output strings, frames, views, trace copies, capacities and byte overhead. The shorter-oriented peak stays at most 9 while the legacy orientation uses 3(m+1) elements.)
\alttext(The preserved-orientation score-storage curve grows with the longer second input, while shorter orientation stays flat for a two-byte first input.)

At a split, the two sweeps evaluate n·m rolling cells. Child rectangles
partition the second range while their first dimensions shrink by about one
half, so their total area decreases geometrically. Together with base scans and
output writing, this gives O(nm+n+m) time, including empty-input output costs.
It does not promise fewer operations than a dense method. Owned full trace
histories add actual retained arrays beyond the untraced storage bound.

> Caps, score bounds and scoring assumptions

The default complete input cap is one million total bytes. The online work cap
is ten million selected rolling DP cells plus base pair scans; each whole sweep
or scan is admitted before its work. Split capture defaults to one million
logical units, charging one record plus 3(m_sub+1) score values per nonbase
split. Whole records are admitted before that call's profile work/capture. Zero
disables each optional policy; the history cap is ignored without tracing. These
are logical counts, not bytes or peak RAM. A failure returns no partial result
and leaves input strings unchanged.

The output uses ASCII '-' as its gap marker, so inputs containing a literal '-'
are rejected. Other bytes, including NUL, compare literally; this is not a
Unicode-codepoint alignment API. Conservative arithmetic admission requires
(n+m) times the largest absolute scoring component to be at most INT_MAX,
preventing overflow even in candidate paths. This may reject an extreme scheme
whose particular optimum would fit. Input/domain checks precede optional caps.
Legacy calls have no optional policy caps and retain their original ties on
admitted inputs.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hirschberg_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto t = dm::algorithms::hirschberg_trace("AB", "BA");
    const auto work = t.run.work.rolling_cells + t.run.work.base_pairs;
    const auto exact =
        dm::algorithms::hirschberg_trace("AB", "BA", {},
                                         {false, 4, work, t.captured_entries});
    bool input =
        false, capture =
        false, budget = false, reserved = false, overflow = false;
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hirschberg_run("AB", "BA", {}, {false, 3, 0, 0});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        input = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hirschberg_trace("AB", "BA", {},
                                                {false, 0, 0,
                                                 t.captured_entries - 1});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        capture = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hirschberg_run("AB", "BA", {},
                                              {false, 0, work - 1, 0});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        budget = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hirschberg("-", "A");
    } catch (const std::invalid_argument &) {
        reserved = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hirschberg("A", "A",
                                          {std::numeric_limits<int>::max(), -1,
                                           -2});
    } catch (const std::overflow_error &) {
        overflow = true;
    }
    std::print("Exact tiny capture {} units; selected work {} cells/scans. One-short input/capture/work " "rejects {}/{}/{}. Reserved gap rejects {}; extreme score rejects {}.\n",
               exact.captured_entries, work, input, capture, budget, reserved,
               overflow);
    const std::string nul_a("A\0B", 3), nul_b("A\0C", 3);
    const auto bytes = dm::algorithms::hirschberg_run(nul_a, nul_b);
    std::print("NUL-byte fixture score {}; output columns {}.\n",
               bytes.alignment.score, bytes.alignment.a_aligned.size());
    std::vector<double> gap, columns;
    std::print("\n| gap score | actual optimal score | actual output columns |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (int g : {-2, 0, 2}) {
        const auto r = dm::algorithms::hirschberg_run("AB", "BA", {2, -1, g});
        gap.push_back(g);
        columns.push_back(r.alignment.a_aligned.size());
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", g, r.alignment.score,
                   r.alignment.a_aligned.size());
    }
    auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    plot.bars(gap, columns, "actual aligned columns", {37, 99, 235}, .8).title(
        "Gap rewards change the mathematical alignment objective").x_label(
        "gap score, with match 2 and mismatch −1").y_label(
        "number of returned alignment columns").y_limits(0, 6).save_svg(
        "build/hirschberg_controls.svg");
    if (!input || !capture || !budget || !reserved || !overflow ||
        bytes.alignment.score != 3)
        throw std::runtime_error("policy controls");
}
```
